cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "polyglot-python"
# Keep `version` in lockstep with pyproject.toml [project].version,
# src/polyglot_python/__init__.py and npm/package.json.
# tests/test_metadata.py enforces this.
version: "0.2.1"
authors:
  - name: "Furox-Art"
    email: "furkanarkn1451@gmail.com"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic multilingual Python keyword transpiler. You keep Python's
  grammar and write programs with localized keywords; polyglot-python maps
  those keywords to the real Python keywords and hands the result to CPython.
  No AI, no network, no randomness: the same source, locale and version always
  produce byte-identical Python. Ships 20 locale tables (ar, de, el, es, fr, hi,
  id, it, ja, ko, nl, pl, pt, ro, ru, sv, tr, uk, vi, zh), a command-line
  interface with run, translate, check, locales and keywords subcommands, and
  no runtime dependencies.
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Furox-Art/polyglot-python"
url: "https://github.com/Furox-Art/polyglot-python"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
